  "worked_solution": "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{|x|}(x+{y}^{2})\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{|x|}(x+{y}^{2})\\,dy]\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{[xy+\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{|x|}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(x\\cdot |x|+\\frac{|x{|}^{3}}{3})dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(x\\cdot |x|+\\frac{|x{|}^{3}}{3})dx & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}(-{x}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})dx+{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})dx \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{12}]}_{-1}^{0}+{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{12}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(0-\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{12})+(\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{12}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
